From a0b3f8c43315c2fd6de94fa4418f9947e615c3a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mytochondria audit <cynthiacondra@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 05:44:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Treat transcripts with undefined GTF strand ('.') as '+' in
 Aligned.toTranscriptome.out.bam and count them from both strands in STARsolo

Transcriptome::quantAlign set the transcriptomic strand with
`trStr==1 ? aG.Str : 1-aG.Str`, so a transcript whose GTF strand is '.'
(stored as 0) was treated like a '-' transcript: the strand flag of every
record was inverted and the sequence reverse-complemented, while
alignToTranscript converts coordinates only for trStr==2, i.e. the
positions were those of the + strand. Such records do not match the
transcript sequence at their position. Undefined-strand transcripts are
now output like + transcripts.

The same expression in Transcriptome::classifyAlign (Gene),
geneFullAlignOverlap (GeneFull), geneFullAlignOverlap_ExonOverIntron and
alignExonOverlap (GeneFull_Ex50pAS) made STARsolo with --soloStrand
Forward drop every sense read of an undefined-strand gene and count them
with --soloStrand Reverse instead (GeneFull_Ex50pAS counted none with
either). Genes with undefined strand now accept reads from both strands
under Forward/Reverse, which is what --quantMode GeneCounts already does
(Transcriptome_geneCountsAddAlign.cpp: "genes w/o strand will accept
reads from both strands").

New regression test extras/tests/scripts/testUndefinedStrand.sh: two
identical two-exon gene structures on '+' and '.', four reads each;
the transcriptome records of the '.' transcript must equal those of
the '+' transcript, and STARsolo --soloStrand Forward must count all
four reads of the '.' gene. Fails on 2.7.11b, passes with this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TaHntBDKuZJpMAAMenkC44
